# The frozen pre-migration wire corpus is byte-exact evidence, so it must check
# out byte-identically on every platform.
#
# `tests/premigration-corpus-integrity.test.ts` hashes each file under this
# directory as a raw `Buffer` and compares the result against a digest recorded
# when the corpus was captured; `tests/premigration-wire-baseline.test.ts`
# replays the same files as the oracle for what the stdio executable puts on the
# wire. Git for Windows installs `core.autocrlf=true` by default, which rewrites
# the recorded LF bytes to CRLF on checkout — so the Windows working tree held
# different bytes and the digest legitimately disagreed there, while the digest
# itself and the single-byte sensitivity control it backs are both correct.
#
# `-text` turns end-of-line conversion off for these paths in both directions,
# which pins the checkout to the recorded bytes without touching the digest and
# without making it line-ending-insensitive.
#
# Scoped to this one directory on purpose: a repository-wide `text=auto eol=lf`
# would renormalise unrelated files in the index, which is a far larger change
# than pinning the evidence this repair is about.
tests/fixtures/premigration/** -text
